","s":310.74,"e":311.02,"line":84},{"w":"hatred","s":311.02,"e":311.57,"line":84},{"w":"decayed.","s":311.57,"e":312.3,"line":84}],"lines":[{"s":1.2,"e":4.16,"text":"DON’T LET THE FUTURE CALL US SAVAGES"},{"s":4.16,"e":7.7,"text":"Children will chronicle the chaos we chose,"},{"s":7.7,"e":11.56,"text":"Counting cold coffins where crimson wind blows."},{"s":11.56,"e":14.93,"text":"Scholars will study the sorrow we spread,"},{"s":14.93,"e":18.31,"text":"Shaming the centuries soaked in the dead."},{"s":18.31,"e":21.18,"text":"Fear feeds fury till families fall,"},{"s":21.18,"e":25.13,"text":"Falsehoods flash brightly, then fracture us all."},{"s":25.13,"e":29.41,"text":"Thoughts turn to threats when we treat them as true,"},{"s":29.41,"e":32.94,"text":"Test them with truth—choose a clearer view."},{"s":32.94,"e":36.81,"text":"Pause, parse the panic; put proof in its place,"},{"s":36.81,"e":40.51,"text":"Breathe before bullets bring blood to a race."},{"s":40.51,"e":44.05,"text":"Name every notion; don’t kneel to its need,"},{"s":44.05,"e":47.58,"text":"Minds make a message—not mandates to bleed."},{"s":47.58,"e":51.53,"text":"Wise minds will whisper where war drums resound,"},{"s":51.53,"e":55.06,"text":"Mercy makes meaning when madness surrounds."},{"s":55.06,"e":59.26,"text":"Feelings are fierce, but they’re fleeting—not fate,"},{"s":59.26,"e":63.78,"text":"Breathe through the blaze before breathing breeds hate."},{"s":63.78,"e":66.82,"text":"DON’T LET THE FUTURE CALL US SAVAGES,"},{"s":66.82,"e":70.77,"text":"Sifting through cities and counting the damages."},{"s":70.77,"e":73.98,"text":"DON’T LET OUR LEGACY LIE IN THE GRAVES,"},{"s":73.98,"e":77.68,"text":"Let it say love made the fearless more brave."},{"s":77.68,"e":81.38,"text":"STOP—SEE THE STORY, THEN SHIFT WHAT IT MEANS,"},{"s":81.38,"e":85.74,"text":"Break brutal beliefs before blood floods the screens."},{"s":85.74,"e":89.36,"text":"Choose conversation, compassion, and change—"},{"s":89.36,"e":92.56,"text":"Don’t let tomorrow remember us strange."},{"s":92.56,"e":96.1,"text":"Pause before power, find peace in the pain,"},{"s":96.1,"e":99.64,"text":"Breathe before borders bring bombers again."},{"s":99.64,"e":102.93,"text":"Heal what we harbor, let hatred be done—"},{"s":102.93,"e":106.46,"text":"One world, one warning, one war left unwon."},{"s":106.46,"e":109.83,"text":"Check every claim when catastrophe calls,"},{"s":109.83,"e":113.7,"text":"Question quick judgments that quarantine walls."},{"s":113.7,"e":117.65,"text":"Facts fight the fiction that fear fashions fast,"},{"s":117.65,"e":121.27,"text":"Present-day peace can repair the cruel past."},{"s":121.27,"e":124.88,"text":"Radical acceptance means seeing what’s real,"},{"s":124.88,"e":128.17,"text":"Not saying slaughter is sacred or steel."},{"s":128.17,"e":131.46,"text":"Accepting the ashes, we act with intent,"},{"s":131.46,"e":135.08,"text":"Building bold bridges where bitterness went."},{"s":135.08,"e":138.37,"text":"Opposite action when anger says “fight,”"},{"s":138.37,"e":141.99,"text":"Listen with love when the loud demand might."},{"s":141.99,"e":145.52,"text":"Regulate rage; let revenge lose its throne,"},{"s":145.52,"e":149.47,"text":"People find peace when their pain becomes known."},{"s":149.47,"e":153.42,"text":"Wise minds will whisper where war drums resound,"},{"s":153.42,"e":156.96,"text":"Mercy makes meaning when madness surrounds."},{"s":156.96,"e":161.15,"text":"Feelings are fierce, but they’re fleeting—not fate,"},{"s":161.15,"e":165.67,"text":"Breathe through the blaze before breathing breeds hate."},{"s":165.67,"e":168.72,"text":"DON’T LET THE FUTURE CALL US SAVAGES,"},{"s":168.72,"e":172.66,"text":"Sifting through cities and counting the damages."},{"s":172.66,"e":175.87,"text":"DON’T LET OUR LEGACY LIE IN THE GRAVES,"},{"s":175.87,"e":179.57,"text":"Let it say love made the fearless more brave."},{"s":179.57,"e":183.27,"text":"STOP—SEE THE STORY, THEN SHIFT WHAT IT MEANS,"},{"s":183.27,"e":187.63,"text":"Break brutal beliefs before blood floods the screens."},{"s":187.63,"e":191.25,"text":"Choose conversation, compassion, and change—"},{"s":191.25,"e":194.46,"text":"Don’t let tomorrow remember us strange."},{"s":194.46,"e":197.91,"text":"Five things I see while the skyline burns,"},{"s":197.91,"e":201.94,"text":"Four things I feel as the frightened world turns."},{"s":201.94,"e":205.97,"text":"Three things I hear through the sirens and cries,"},{"s":205.97,"e":209.83,"text":"Two things I smell beneath smoke-covered skies."},{"s":209.83,"e":213.62,"text":"One thing I taste: bitter tears turning brave,"},{"s":213.62,"e":216.99,"text":"Grounded, we gather the goodness we save."},{"s":216.99,"e":220.85,"text":"Distress can be carried; destruction can cease,"},{"s":220.85,"e":224.47,"text":"Pain can be present while people pick peace."},{"s":224.47,"e":228.34,"text":"Soldiers are sons, and the strangers are souls,"},{"s":228.34,"e":232.2,"text":"Mothers mourn mothers when missiles meet goals."},{"s":232.2,"e":236.23,"text":"Leaders must learn what the wounded already know:"},{"s":236.23,"e":239.6,"text":"Victory vanishes when violence must grow."},{"s":239.6,"e":243.3,"text":"Future-born families will find what we wrote,"},{"s":243.3,"e":246.43,"text":"Reading our reasons in ruin and smoke."},{"s":246.43,"e":250.54,"text":"Will they call courage the course that we charted—"},{"s":250.54,"e":254.41,"text":"Or call us barbarians, brilliant but heartless?"},{"s":254.41,"e":257.45,"text":"DON’T LET THE FUTURE CALL US SAVAGES,"},{"s":257.45,"e":261.4,"text":"Sifting through cities and counting the damages."},{"s":261.4,"e":264.6,"text":"DON’T LET OUR LEGACY LIE IN THE GRAVES,"},{"s":264.6,"e":268.3,"text":"Let it say love made the fearless more brave."},{"s":268.3,"e":272,"text":"STOP—SEE THE STORY, THEN SHIFT WHAT IT MEANS,"},{"s":272,"e":276.36,"text":"Break brutal beliefs before blood floods the screens."},{"s":276.36,"e":279.98,"text":"Choose conversation, compassion, and change—"},{"s":279.98,"e":283.19,"text":"Don’t let tomorrow remember us strange."},{"s":283.19,"e":286.56,"text":"MAKE MINDFUL MERCY THE MARK THAT REMAINS,"},{"s":286.56,"e":290.34,"text":"Turn trauma to treaties and prisons to plains."},{"s":290.34,"e":293.8,"text":"Let future generations look lovingly back—"},{"s":293.8,"e":298.32,"text":"And say we found peace when the whole world went black."},{"s":298.32,"e":301.44,"text":"History hears every heartbeat we save,"},{"s":301.44,"e":305.31,"text":"Peace is the proof that the powerful are brave."},{"s":305.31,"e":309.09,"text":"Children will cherish the choice that we made:"},{"s":309.09,"e":312.3,"text":"Humanity healed—and the hatred decayed."}],"duration":312.8,"source":"estimated","generatedAt":null}